<h2>What Base64 does</h2><p>Base64 represents binary data using a limited text alphabet. It is common in data URLs, email transport, APIs and formats that need binary-safe text representation.</p><h2>How to use this encoder and decoder</h2><ol><li>Paste ordinary text and choose Encode to produce Base64.</li><li>Paste a Base64 string and choose Decode to recover UTF-8 text.</li><li>Copy the output as needed.</li></ol><h2>Why UTF-8 handling matters</h2><p>Browser <code>btoa</code> and <code>atob</code> operate on byte-oriented strings. This tool uses <code>TextEncoder</code> and <code>TextDecoder</code> so characters such as emoji and non-English scripts are converted correctly.</p><h2>Base64 does not secure data</h2><p>Encoding is reversible and requires no secret key. Never treat a Base64 string as encrypted, hashed or confidential.</p>
<?php $toolContent=ob_get_clean();$faqs=[['Is Base64 encryption?','No. Base64 is a reversible encoding format and provides no confidentiality.'],['Can this tool handle emoji and Unicode text?','Yes. It converts text through UTF-8 bytes before encoding and after decoding.'],['Why does Base64 output look longer?','Base64 represents binary data using text characters and generally adds size overhead compared with the original bytes.'],['Is the input uploaded?','No. Encoding and decoding in this release run in your browser.']];require __DIR__.'/../includes/tool-template.php';
